# dsv41: spill v2 on the pair (port of GLM 0110 on 0088, MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#124 and
# #78): every kept prompt state of --spill-min-tokens or more is written to each rank's own local disk when it is kept,
# through 0013's store and 0014's Tier, and read back beside decoding streams when a request extends it, also after a
# restart or a crash.
# - spill_state.zig: what a point holds on one rank: the compressed and index planes in 2048-token blocks (890 B a
#   token a rank) and the small state (the window rings, the raw stores), derived from the loaded layers and checked
#   against the live allocation; Packer copies between the planes and pinned staging; the rules for what is rebuilt
#   instead of stored (drafter rings, the Engram read-ahead).
# - rank_wire.zig (lanes Kind 10): the ranks' sub-protocol (hello, agreed, has, reserve, start, progress, commit,
#   abort), ordered by a Tracker, every reply bounded. fingerprint.zig and rank_identity.zig: a SHA-256 per field of
#   what the bytes depend on (engine, recipe patches, model and Engram revisions, each rank's weight file by its footer
#   index and recorded digest, the layout, the features; the chat template per rank, the host CPU model left out),
#   agreed at start; a mismatch refuses, naming the rank and the field, and frees the frames the hello wrote.
# - spill_tier.zig: rank 0's Leader (the Tier) and the followers' side; the wiring in lanes, native and lanes_main;
#   pinned staging (TF_DS_SPILL_STAGING_MIB, 128) allocated before the pool is sized.
# Switches: rank 0 --spill-dir DIR and --spill-gib N (off), --spill-min-free-gib 50, --spill-min-tokens 8192 (in the
# fingerprint: equal on both ranks), --spill-quota 0; followers TF_DS_SPILL_DIR, TF_DS_SPILL_GIB,
# TF_DS_SPILL_MIN_FREE_GIB, TF_DS_SPILL_MIN_TOKENS, TF_DS_SPILL_QUOTA; the identity TF_DS_ENGINE_ID,
# TF_DS_RECIPE_PATCHES, TF_DS_MODEL_REVISION, TF_DS_ENGRAM_REVISION, TF_DS_RANK_CACHE_SHA, TF_DS_BUILD_FLAGS,
# TF_DS_ABLATION_ID (the recipe sets them: scripts/port.sh, SPILL_GIB). The pair only (TF_TP_WORLD=2); with
# TF_DS_KV_SHARD=1 the tier is refused (SpillWithKvShard) until 0019. Off: no staging, no fingerprint, no Kind 10
# frame, the lanes stream's bytes unchanged.
# Measured on the pair (engine 9983b2f, before the rebase onto 0008, SPILL_GIB=64): exact.py 39/39 identical;
# tools/spill_check PASS 22 checks, 0 failed, 1 skipped (12 seeds of 5 to 100K tokens committed on both ranks; an
# evicted 14,336-token state restored from disk exact; a corrupt, truncated or removed file on either rank refused and
# recomputed exact; two restores while decoding 2.79 s; after a restart the points recovered and a restore exact);
# decode and prefill within noise of spill off (-2.7 to +3.5 %).
# Block layout, lineage, write-at-keep ring, release and fsync order: BadAd84's block-tier design
# (MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#118); the rest by Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Builds on
# 0013, 0014 and 0015 (the planner's types and the KV-shard settings). Apache-2.0.
